ir: ♣9 ♦9\nsingle: ♥7\nsingle: ♣8\nsingle: ♣9\nsingle: ♦J\nsingle: ♣Q\ntriple: ♥9 ♣9 ♦9\ntriple_with_pair: ♥7 ♦7 ♥9 ♣9 ♦9\ntriple_with_single: ♥7 ♥9 ♣9 ♦9\ntriple_with_single: ♣8 ♥9 ♣9 ♦9\ntriple_with_single: ♥9 ♣9 ♦9 ♦J\ntriple_with_single: ♥9 ♣9 ♦9 ♣Q\n\nSelect the best move from the Valid Moves list above. You can choose to pass even if you have valid moves that can beat the previous play, but you cannot pass if you are in a Free Play (no last play).\nEnsure your response matches one of the valid moves exactly.\nRemember to provide Explanation, Reason, and Answer.", 'reasoning': '', 'output': 'Evaluation: With free play, the fastest path is to shed cards in bigger combos. The strongest tempo moves here are **triple_with_pair (full house)** for 5 cards, or **triple_with_single** for 4 cards. Leading a mere pair or single is slower and gives peasants more chances to overtake/empty (Prev has only 5 cards left). Using **♥7 ♦7** as the attached pair is efficient because it leaves you with three clean singles (♣8 ♦J ♣Q) after the 5-card play.\n\nReason: Play **♥7 ♦7 ♥9 ♣9 ♦9** to dump 5 cards immediately and simplify your remaining hand to easy singles, minimizing the risk of being out-raced by the left peasant with 5 cards.\n\nAnswer: {"cards":["♥7","♦7","♥9","♣9","♦9"]}'}
